Significant changes made by Kizuna relative to upstream Mihon include:
  - Addition of a "novel" content type alongside Mihon's existing
    image-based (manga/manhwa/manhua) content type in the source/extension
    system, including an embedded JS engine for running novel extension
    sources.
  - A new native text reader for novel content, separate from Mihon's
    existing image pager/webtoon readers.
  - A unified library, browse/extensions screen, and app-wide mode toggle
    spanning both content types.
  - An entry-linking feature connecting image and novel entries that are
    adaptations of one another.
  - Rebranding of application identifiers (app name, application ID) from
    Mihon to Kizuna.

